		{"id":"3a5a1edadb615117","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(1991) Gulf War.md","x":109,"y":21481,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b4c2f63a001b587f","type":"text","text":"Desert Storm\nDesert Storm was the code name for the military campaign that took place during the Gulf War in 1991. The campaign involved a coalition of international forces, including the United States, Saudi Arabia, and other countries, who united to drive Iraq out of Kuwait and restore Kuwait's independence. The coalition used a combination of air strikes and ground forces to advance into Iraq and liberate Kuwait. The ground campaign was highly successful, with the Iraqi military collapsing in the face of the overwhelming coalition forces. Desert Storm was one of the most successful military campaigns in modern history, with minimal casualties and significant strategic and tactical gains for the coalition. It also marked a significant victory for the United States and its allies in the Cold War, demonstrating their ability to respond decisively to regional crises. Despite its success, Desert Storm also had significant political and humanitarian consequences, including the displacement of millions of people and the destruction of much of Iraq's infrastructure. It also contributed to the ongoing tensions between the United States and Iraq, which have persisted into the present day.\n","x":589,"y":21357,"width":525,"height":524},
		{"id":"e7f8edf4cf752a6a","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(1991) Fall of the USSR.md","x":109,"y":21881,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5ea2bc51d8ca43c5","type":"text","text":"End of the Cold War\nAt the close of the cold war, a KGB agent had defected to the west and came with a warning, a war of subversion is under way. A battle of ideas that would reshape the nation from within. While the news would be alarming it fell on deaf ears and result in decades of uncheck subversion and indoctrination.\n","x":650,"y":21975,"width":403,"height":213},
		{"id":"3433f0409aa3d3d9","type":"text","text":"Collapse of The Nuclear Family\nThe goal of socialism is to create a society that is controlled by the state, and the destruction of traditional family structures is a key part of this agenda. By promoting the sexual revolution and targeting minority groups, socialists aim to create a society where individuals are more vulnerable to manipulation and indoctrination.\nThe end result is a society where traditional values are replaced with a radical, socialist ideology, and where individuals lack familial support. This creates a vacuum that can be filled by the state, and the result is a society that is deeply reliant on the state for guidance and support.\nIt is crucial to recognize these attempts at subversion and to protect traditional family structures and values. We must stand against the efforts of socialists to dismantle the family and promote a one-size-fits-all, state-controlled society.\n","x":-691,"y":19081,"width":289,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"36b477dab4fd7574","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(1999) Viral therapy.md","x":-320,"y":21481,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"faa6959cb3ae217f","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2000) Psycho genesis.md","x":-320,"y":21882,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0f6dce7516cb7ec1","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2001) Crisis.md","x":109,"y":22282,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"64e9a98270237ab9","type":"text","text":"War on Terror\nThe war on terror is an ongoing campaign launched by the United States and its allies in response to the September 11 attacks of 2001 and other terrorist attacks worldwide. The campaign involves a range of measures, including military intervention, intelligence gathering, and counterterrorism efforts. The war on terror has been characterized by intense debate over its effectiveness, cost, and morality. Some argue that the campaign has failed to achieve its goals of defeating terrorism and protecting American security, while others argue that it has made significant progress in disrupting terrorist networks and reducing the threat of attack. The war on terror has also been criticized for its reliance on military force and the potential for collateral damage, as well as its impact on civil liberties and the rule of law. It has also sparked tensions between the United States and other countries, particularly those affected by drone strikes and other military actions. Despite these criticisms, the war on terror remains a key issue in American politics and international relations, as the United States and its allies continue to confront the threat of global terrorism and extremism.\n","x":650,"y":22216,"width":515,"height":533},
		{"id":"86d57104c90331fb","type":"text","text":"Socialization of Europe\nIf the EU were described as corrupt to the core with communist ideology, it would imply that the EU's decision-making process and institutions are controlled by a system of corruption that supports and promotes communist ideology. This would mean that the EU's goals and objectives are aligned with the principles of communism, which emphasize the collective ownership and management of resources and a rejection of individual property rights. It would also suggest that the EU's policies and regulations are biased towards promoting communist values and practices, such as state ownership of industries, government control over the economy, and socialist redistribution of wealth. Such a description would likely be seen as highly critical and negative, and would be based on accusations of collusion between EU officials and communist or left-wing groups to advance their agenda. It would also imply a complete lack of transparency and accountability within the EU's decision-making process, with corruption permeating all levels of EU institutions. This would lead to a lack of trust in the EU as an organization, as well as widespread concerns about the legitimacy of its policies and decisions. It would also create tensions with other EU member states that do not share these values or beliefs, leading to political divisions and fragmentation within the EU.\n","x":1240,"y":22202,"width":536,"height":561},
		{"id":"76f399fdb26ca23e","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2008) Equal rights (as an illusion) (monopoly on physical force).md","x":109,"y":22682,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"aa1961f524f49edb","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2008) Economic Depression.md","x":109,"y":23082,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
