		{"id":"d1b5531160139ae5","type":"text","text":"The Great Conspiracy\nThe great conspiracy is a plot between multiple stations within the government branches and various agencies to maintain and exert control through legislation and rule of law while disregarding its foundations.\n","x":602,"y":23536,"width":250,"height":293},
		{"id":"573c2c5fcff6737a","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2011) Manhunt.md","x":109,"y":23882,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"9272a4b5e86989e1","type":"text","text":"KGB Defector\n1. KGB/FSB DEFECTOR DOSSIER\n\nFILE: ARSENYEV, MIKHAIL SERGEEVICH\nStatus: Presumed dead, 2011. Unconfirmed.\nDOB: 23 April 1962\nOrigin: Leningrad, USSR\nRank: Colonel (KGB) → Senior Analyst (FSB successor)\nSpecialty: Ideological counter-intelligence, foreign infiltration analysis\nYears Active: 1984–2008\nNationality: Russian (defected 2008)\n\nSummary\n\nA brilliant but politically vulnerable KGB/FSB analyst whose job was to track foreign ideological penetration. Ironically, this made him one of the only Soviet officers to understand how deeply the USSR had infiltrated Western institutions over decades — and how such networks, once created, persist even when the original state collapses.\n\nWhen his faction lost influence inside the post-Russian intelligence hierarchy, he fled to the West as a self-interested defector… then realized the West lacked the willpower or self-awareness to understand the threat he carried.\n\nHe became a prophet no one listened to.\n\n⸻\n\n2. PSYCHOLOGICAL PROFILE\n\n(MI6/CIA Joint Psychological Evaluation — 2009)\n\nPersonality Type:\n\t•\tPragmatic\n\t•\tCynical\n\t•\tHigh-functioning paranoid\n\t•\tExtremely observant\n\t•\tEmotionally flattened\n\t•\tMorally fluid\n\t•\tLoyalty is tactical, not ideological\n\nKey Traits:\n\t•\tPossesses pattern cognition well above average\n\t•\tAvoids all emotional language\n\t•\tTreats geopolitics as a natural science\n\t•\tExpresses contempt for idealists on all sides\n\t•\tDoes not see nations — sees systems\n\t•\tDescribes Western democracy as “a house infested with termites”\n\nRisk Assessment:\n\t•\tNot a psychopath\n\t•\tBut empathy is compartmentalized\n\t•\tHas a survivor mindset\n\t•\tWill lie if cornered\n\t•\tWill tell the truth if it benefits him\n\nFinal Analyst Note:\n\n“Arsenyev is valuable because he does not care about belonging.\nHe does not want to save us — he wants to be heard.”\n\n⸻\n\n3. FIRST DEBRIEF TRANSCRIPT\n\nExtract — Langley Safehouse, 14 March 2009\nAgents present: H. Coleridge (CIA), A. Malcolm (MI6)\nArsenyev is exhausted, dehydrated, but lucid.\n\n⸻\n\nColeridge: “Colonel Arsenyev. Why defect now?”\n\nArsenyev: “Because I want to live. I assume that is still allowed in your country.”\n\nMalcolm: “You’re in no danger here. We need to understand what you know.”\n\nArsenyev: “You need to understand what you already lost.”\n\n(Pause)\n\nColeridge: “Explain.”\n\nArsenyev:\n\n“You believe the Soviet Union collapsed. It did not. It metastasized.”\n\nMalcolm: “Meaning what, exactly?”\n\nArsenyev:\n\n“Your institutions — academia, media, finance, culture — you believed they were infiltrated by accident.\nNo. They were cultivated. Seeds planted in the 1970s, grown in the 1990s, now flowering.”\n\nColeridge: “And this is related to Operation Anvil?”\n\nArsenyev: (leans forward)\n\n“Operation Anvil was not a military plan.\nIt was an ideological slow knife.”\n\nMalcolm: “You’re suggesting the operation still exists?”\n\nArsenyev:\n\n“Not Soviet. Not Russian.\nSomething worse.\nSomething that no longer needs Moscow at all.”\n\nColeridge: “What is it then?”\n\nArsenyev:\n\n“Call it what you like.\nMy people called it divnyy budushchiy mir — the ‘wonderful future world.’\nYour people will call it ‘global progress.’\nIt is the same thing.”\n\n(Long silence)\n\nArsenyev:\n\n“You think you are being conquered.\nYou are not.\nYou are being replaced.”\n\n⸻\n\n4. WHAT ARSENYEV REVEALS ABOUT OPERATION ANVIL\n\nOperation Anvil was never about war.\n\nIt was about permanent ideological leverage.\n\nHe exposes seven pillars:\n\n1. Cultural Infiltration\n\n1968–1995\nBuild activist networks → let them radicalize naturally → feed them theoretical fuel → let Western institutions adopt them as “modern values.”\n\n2. Academic Capture\n\n1975–2005\nSeed Western universities with carefully groomed foreign theorists whose ideas erode national identity and redefine authority.\n\n3. Media Narrative Drift\n\n1980–2000\nTrain sympathetic journalists and thinkers → export them → let them “Westernize” the propaganda.\n\n4. Bureaucratic Embedding\n\n1985–2010\nMoles aren’t spies — they’re administrators shaping long-term policy.\n\n5. Economic Entanglement\n\n1990–2008\nPush globalization → weaken national sovereignty → create dependency on transnational elites.\n\n6. Psychological Destabilization\n\n2001–2020\nTrauma + surveillance + digital addiction produces a population too exhausted to resist.\n\n7. Institutional Hollowing\n\n2008–2035\nDemocracies become rituals.\nPower becomes opaque.\nElections change nothing.\n\nOperation Anvil is about making the West collapse without a single shot fired.\n\nArsenyev’s Warning (Canonical)\n\n“The danger is not the communists you fear.\nThe danger is the communists who forgot they were communists.”\n\nThis directly sets up your Globalist vs. Nationalist Civil War.\n\n⸻\n\n5. HIS DISAPPEARANCE (2011)\n\nOfficial Story\n\nHeart attack in a Virginia hotel.\n\nUnofficial Theories\n\t•\tCIA black site extraction\n\t•\teliminated by Russian hit team\n\t•\tabsorbed into Operation Home Run pre-planning\n\t•\tdefected again to a third faction\n\t•\tvoluntary disappearance under a new identity\n\t•\tkilled by Europolis agents years later\n\nMost Likely Canon\n\nHe was taken by a Western deep-state cell that realized he was a liability.\nHis final warnings were too accurate.\nToo aligned with the rising nationalist faction.\n\nHe was buried quietly.\nOr protected quietly.\n\nEither way, he was removed from the story.\n\n⸻\n\n6. RESULTING CONSPIRACIES ABOUT HIM\n\nAfter 2020, Arsenyev becomes a mythic figure:\n\t•\t“the man who saw the collapse coming”\n\t•\t“the KGB prophet”\n\t•\t“the father of Operation Home Run”\n\t•\t“the ghost of Operation Anvil”\n\t•\t“the man who tried to stop Europolis before it was born”\n\nRadical factions use his name.\nNationalists revere him.\nGlobalists deny he existed.\nCRINK sees him as a cautionary tale.\nCIA archives on him remain sealed.\n\n⸻\n\n7. HIS IMPACT ON THE ALT-EARTH TIMELINE\n\nDirect Effects\n\t•\tOperation Home Run draws heavily on his intel\n\t•\tnationalist factions use his predictions as blueprints\n\t•\tCRINK accelerates countermeasures\n\t•\tEuropolis models its societal structure on what he warned about\n\t•\trelic destabilization research uses his early cognitive anomaly reports\n\t•\tSeverance-era psychological models cite his notes on identity fracture\n\nIndirect Effects\n\t•\tthe U.S. Civil War (Globalists vs. Constitutionalists) is foreshadowed in his warnings\n\t•\tthe globalization collapse appears exactly as he predicted\n\t•\tthe post-2035 elite technocracy matches his fears\n\t•\tdestabilization of cognitive baselines mirrors his forecasts\n\t•\this notes on “ideological drift” become prophetic\n\t•\thistorians consider him the first man to notice Aether-adjacent bleedthrough\n\nHe becomes the John the Baptist of your divergent Earth.\n\nThe man who warned the world and watched it walk to its own execution.\n","x":-580,"y":23841,"width":520,"height":482},
		{"id":"147dec5a41b7f4f2","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2000) Bio suspension.md","x":-720,"y":21881,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e4bd4debfaa575d0","type":"text","text":"Terror Escalation\nTerror escalation occurs when a group of terrorists engages in increasingly violent and deadly attacks, often as a response to government repression or perceived injustices. As the group escalates its attacks, the level of violence and destruction typically increases, leading to greater fear and anxiety among the public. This fear can in turn create a cycle of violence, where the government responds to the escalating attacks with greater force and security measures, which in turn may provoke further attacks from the terrorists. Terror escalation can be triggered by a variety of factors, including political or social unrest, economic hardship, religious or ethnic tensions, or repression by authorities. It can also be influenced by factors such as the availability of weapons, resources, and intelligence networks, as well as the motivation and leadership of the terrorists themselves. In many cases, terror escalation can lead to a spiral of violence that is difficult to stop, as each side becomes increasingly radicalized and entrenched in its position. This can have far-reaching consequences for society and the state, leading to widespread destruction, loss of life, and damage to infrastructure and public services. To prevent terror escalation, it is important for governments to address underlying causes of conflict and unrest, and to implement policies that prioritize the protection of civil liberties and human rights. It is also essential to engage in dialogue with all parties involved, and to pursue non-violent solutions whenever possible.","x":625,"y":23882,"width":566,"height":610},
		{"id":"eaa766576c14ff5a","type":"text","text":"Weaponized Organizations\nWeaponized organizations and hate groups are groups or individuals who use violence or other forms of coercion to further their ideological or political goals. These groups are often motivated by hate, intolerance, and a desire for power or dominance over others. Weaponized organizations and hate groups can take many forms, including terrorist organizations, paramilitary groups, and extremist factions. They may target specific groups or individuals based on their race, religion, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, or other characteristics. These groups often use propaganda and social media to recruit and radicalize members, and they may engage in activities such as propaganda campaigns, attacks on public figures, and cyber attacks. They may also have financial support from wealthy individuals or political organizations, which can help them to operate and grow. The consequences of weaponized organizations and hate groups can be devastating, including loss of life, property damage, and fear and instability in affected communities. Their actions can also undermine the rule of law and erode trust in democratic institutions, which can have far-reaching effects on society. Therefore, it is crucial to identify and counter these groups through intelligence gathering, law enforcement efforts, and prevention strategies such as public education and community outreach.\n","x":1264,"y":23882,"width":512,"height":639},
		{"id":"ce781d7cdb33d7e5","type":"text","text":"Political Corruption\nThe corruption of politicians is key to demoralize and deconstruct a nation. Corrupt corporations also practiced in buying politicians to pass legislation that furthers the agenda of the socialist agenda.\n","x":941,"y":23536,"width":250,"height":277},
		{"id":"8990a076d8b71623","type":"text","text":"Food Pyramid Conspiracy\nThere have been various conspiracy theories that suggest that the food pyramid was deliberately designed to artificially create an obesity epidemic in the United States. According to these theories, the government and large food corporations were involved in a conspiracy to promote the consumption of processed and high-calorie foods, such as sugary snacks and fried meats, at the expense of healthier options like fruits and vegetables. One of the main reasons given for this conspiracy is that it would benefit the government and food corporations financially. By promoting the consumption of cheap, processed foods, they could increase their profits and maintain their market dominance. Furthermore, some conspiracy theorists suggest that the food pyramid was deliberately designed to be confusing and difficult to understand, in order to encourage people to turn to processed foods as a shortcut to meeting their daily nutritional needs. In addition, it has been argued that the government's recommendations for healthy eating were largely ignored or overridden by the powerful food industry, leading to a lack of regulation and enforcement of healthy food. there is some truth to the idea that processed foods are more easily accessible and cheaper than healthy options, and that this has contributed to the rise in obesity rates in recent years.","x":1264,"y":23082,"width":483,"height":644},
		{"id":"c3cf657ab1e22ef5","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2020) The Plagues.md","x":109,"y":24282,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"04b28a9dda66d1fa","type":"text","text":"Bio Tests\nBiological testing on human subjects is any research that involves the use of human beings as subjects for experiments, treatments, or other medical interventions. While scientific research can lead to important advances in medicine and health, it can also pose ethical challenges, particularly when it involves the exploitation of vulnerable populations or the sacrifice of human life. One form of unethical biological testing on human subjects is human experimentation. This involves the use of humans as test subjects without their informed consent or without the provision of adequate compensation, medical care, or other support. Human experimentation was a common practice during the Holocaust, when Nazi doctors conducted cruel and inhumane experiments on prisoners at concentration camps. Another form of unethical biological testing on human subjects is the use of vulnerable populations as subjects. This includes individuals who are unable to give informed consent due to age, mental illness, poverty, or other factors. Such populations may be exploited by research institutions or corporations seeking to maximize profits or minimize ethical concerns. A third form of unethical biological testing on human subjects is the conduct of research that poses an unacceptable risk to the health or safety of the subjects. This can include testing experimental drugs or treatments on people who have a high risk of contracting a disease or who are not well-suited to participate in a clinical trial. In conclusion, unethical biological testing on human subjects can lead to serious harm and exploitation of vulnerable populations. It is important to ensure that such research is conducted in accordance with ethical principles and regulatory standards, and that the rights and welfare of human subjects are always given priority.\n","x":-320,"y":24359,"width":334,"height":405},
		{"id":"68f5110f2f892f06","type":"text","text":"Virus\nThe development and use of lab-made viruses can be seen as an unethical practice for several reasons. Here are some examples of such practices: 1. Unethical motives: Lab-made viruses can be developed for the purpose of creating biological weapons or as a means of achieving political or economic objectives. Such motives are often driven by self-interest or the pursuit of power, rather than the advancement of science or the benefit of humanity. 2. Risk to public health: Lab-made viruses can pose a significant risk to public health if they are released intentionally or accidentally. This can result in the spread of deadly diseases and a loss of life. 3. Disregard for human ethics: The creation and use of lab-made viruses can violate the ethical principles of respect for life, non-maleficence, and justice. They can be seen as violating the rights of individuals and society as a whole. 4. Violation of international treaties: Many countries have signed international treaties that prohibit the development and use of certain types of weapons, including bioweapons. The creation and use of lab-made viruses could therefore be seen as a violation of these treaties and an act of aggression against other nations. 5. Limited scientific benefit: The scientific benefits of lab-made viruses are often limited, as their primary purpose is to cause harm or create fear and intimidation. This can detract from the development of more beneficial and effective treatments or therapies that could save lives and improve human health. In conclusion, unethical lab-made viruses pose significant risks to public health, human rights, and international peace and security. They are a product of self-interest and political motivations, rather than scientific advancement, and should be viewed with caution and skepticism by both the scientific community and society at large.\n","x":-737,"y":24362,"width":315,"height":402},
		{"id":"f6da2bc8c4d69d31","type":"text","text":"Sudo Vaccination\nSudo vaccinations, or vaccine scams, are unethical practices that take advantage of people's trust in vaccines and the healthcare system to profit from selling fake or ineffective vaccines. Here are some examples of sudo vaccinations: 1. Vaccine scams: Scammers may advertise bogus vaccines that claim to provide protection against certain diseases. They may also sell vaccines that have been altered or contaminated, making them less effective or potentially dangerous. 2. Fake vaccine clinics: Criminals may set up fake vaccine clinics in impoverished or underdeveloped areas, charging people exorbitant fees for vaccinations that do not provide any protection. 3. Overcharging: Some healthcare providers may overcharge for vaccinations, taking advantage of the fact that patients often do not fully understand the costs associated with healthcare services. 4. Bundling vaccines with unnecessary procedures: Some providers may offer vaccines as part of a package deal, requiring patients to undergo other procedures that they do not need or want. This can be a way to inflate the price of vaccinations and increase profits. 5. Lack of transparency: Scammers and unethical providers may lack transparency about the composition and effectiveness of the vaccines they are selling or administering. This can make it difficult for patients to make informed decisions about their healthcare. Sudo vaccinations pose significant risks to public health, as they can spread misinformation about the safety and efficacy of vaccines and prevent people from receiving important immunizations. They also contribute to the financial exploitation of vulnerable populations, making it harder for them to access affordable and effective healthcare.\n","x":-359,"y":24821,"width":413,"height":429},
		{"id":"4bf412564b72e5ce","type":"text","text":"Outbreaks\nA disease outbreak occurs when a large number of people become sick with a particular illness or disease at the same time. Disease outbreaks can be caused by a number of factors, including: 1. Inadequate public health measures: If public health measures such as vaccinations or hygiene practices are not implemented or enforced, outbreaks can occur. 2. Climate change: Extreme weather events, such as hurricanes or floods, can disrupt water supplies and sanitation systems, leading to the spread of disease. 3. Travel: International travel can spread infectious diseases between different populations. 4. Contaminated food or water: Foodborne illnesses and waterborne diseases can cause outbreaks if contaminated with harmful microorganisms. In contrast, sudo outbreaks are deliberate attempts to create the appearance of a disease outbreak. These scams may involve contaminating food or water supplies or releasing diseased animals or insects into the environment. Sudo outbreaks can be carried out by individuals or groups with a range of motives, including financial gain, political agendas, or simply causing chaos and panic. Sudo outbreaks are often more dangerous than true disease outbreaks, as they can cause widespread fear and paranoia, leading to incorrect treatment decisions and overuse of medical resources.\n","x":-769,"y":24849,"width":379,"height":416},
		{"id":"337a7eec4bbef1e5","type":"text","text":"National Quarantines\nNational quarantines are public health measures that involve the isolation of individuals or entire communities to prevent the spread of infectious diseases. They are often implemented during disease outbreaks to contain the virus and protect the health of the general population. Real national quarantines are often a necessary response to serious health emergencies, such as pandemic flu outbreaks or highly contagious diseases like Ebola. During such quarantines, individuals who have been exposed to the disease are isolated from the rest of the population until they have been deemed safe to rejoin society. This can include restrictions on travel, contact with others, and access to public facilities. Sudo national quarantines, on the other hand, are deliberately created to cause panic and disruption. They may involve fabricated reports of disease outbreaks or misleading information about the severity of the situation. Sudo national quarantines can be particularly harmful, as they can lead to hoarding of essential supplies, shortages of medical resources, and other economic and social disruptions. The difference between real and sudo national quarantines is often difficult to distinguish, as both can involve similar public health measures and cause significant harm to individuals and communities. It is important for governments and healthcare professionals to be vigilant in distinguishing between legitimate health concerns and sudo outbreaks, and to implement appropriate measures to protect public health without causing unnecessary fear or panic.\n","x":-1200,"y":24920,"width":372,"height":457},
		{"id":"90cc3d2f9735673a","type":"text","text":"Draconian Lockdowns\nThe use of national quarantines as a tool to enact a police state is a serious and dangerous possibility. When used for this purpose, quarantines can be implemented in a way that severely restricts individual freedoms and limits the ability of citizens to exercise their rights and responsibilities as members of a democratic society. For example, real national quarantines may be used as a pretext to justify the deployment of excessive military or police resources, the surveillance and tracking of individuals, and the imposition of harsh penalties for non-compliance. These measures can erode civil liberties and undermine the democratic principles of accountability and transparency. Sudo national quarantines, on the other hand, can be used to promote a false sense of emergency and urgency that justifies even more draconian measures. For instance, authorities may claim that it is necessary to impose harsh restrictions on movement or communication in order to prevent the spread of disease, when in reality there may be other factors at play. In either case, the use of national quarantines as a tool to enact a police state is fundamentally flawed. Such measures undermine the trust between citizens and their governments, erode public health and safety, and ultimately harm the very populations they are intended to protect. It is important for governments to approach public health crises with transparency, compassion, and accountability, and to resist the temptation to resort to authoritarianism in the face of uncertainty.\n","x":-1230,"y":24334,"width":402,"height":459},
		{"id":"adcf02a27f0d9e68","type":"text","text":"The Red Wave\nThe red wave also known as the socialist wave was a tipping point within the American sphere when far-left leaning philosophies took a firm grip upon the highest institutions of the free world.\n","x":941,"y":24563,"width":322,"height":204},
		{"id":"89f99c3e3e19e1e1","type":"text","text":"The Shadow State\nThe Shadow State is a clandestine organization that operates in the darkest corners of the US government. It is a secretive and powerful entity that is shrouded in mystery and fear. The Shadow State has been manipulating the political system from within for decades, using its vast resources and influence to control key institutions and individuals. Its ultimate goal is to ensure total control over all aspects of the nation, from foreign policy to domestic affairs. The Shadow State operates through a network of agents and operatives, many of whom are embedded deep within the government's bureaucracy. They are known for their ruthlessness and their willingness to use any means necessary to achieve their goals, including covert operations, assassinations, and the suppression of dissent. Despite their secretive nature, the existence of the Shadow State is well known among those who are in the know. There are whispers of its power and influence, and some even speculate that it has infiltrated every level of government, from the highest levels of national security to the local police force. Those who resist the Shadow State's agenda face a formidable foe. The organization is not afraid to use its vast resources to eliminate threats, and its agents are skilled in manipulation, blackmail, and intimidation. The fight against the Shadow State is long and difficult, as it operates from the shadows and has a seemingly endless supply of resources. But for those who are willing to stand up against it, the battle will continue, with the fate of the nation hanging in the balance.\n","x":1321,"y":24635,"width":369,"height":373},
		{"id":"960f279464d3876c","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2020) Private thought.md","x":509,"y":24682,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"89d4c8606b4b994c","type":"text","text":"Decades of Waste\nThe pulling out of Afghanistan refers to the process of U.S. military forces withdrawing from the country, which began in May 2021 after nearly two decades of war. The U.S. involvement in Afghanistan began in 2001 following the September 11 attacks, when President George W. Bush authorized a military intervention in Afghanistan to overthrow the Taliban regime, which was harboring Osama bin Laden and other al-Qaeda leaders. Over the course of the next two decades, the United States and its allies engaged in a long and costly conflict in Afghanistan, which was marked by significant setbacks and controversial tactics. The war resulted in the deaths of thousands of U.S. soldiers and Afghan civilians, as well as the destruction of much of Afghanistan's infrastructure and economy. In May 2021, President Joe Biden announced a plan to withdraw all U.S. troops from Afghanistan by September 11th, marking the end of the U.S. military presence in the country after nearly two decades of conflict. The withdrawal was met with mixed reactions from Afghan officials and citizens, with some hailing it as a sign of progress and a chance for peace, while others expressed concerns about the future stability of the country and the risk of Taliban control. Today, the Taliban has taken control of most of Afghanistan and has imposed strict restrictions on women's rights and freedoms. As a result, many Afghans are fleeing the country in search of safety, while others are concerned about the impact of the Taliban government on their lives and livelihoods.","x":-549,"y":25377,"width":458,"height":526},
		{"id":"bf6af017467f6157","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2030) Existence.md","x":991,"y":25149,"width":400,"height":400},
