		{"id":"3c06edbbde1513a1","type":"text","text":"The Shot Heard Round the World\nWith the mass arrests and raids, eventually events would spiral out of control. Boston massachusetts would be ground zero for the first act of true violence when a group of nationalists are rounded up at beacon hill and executed. \n","x":665,"y":28181,"width":343,"height":205},
		{"id":"779a64358fd337a8","type":"text","text":"The 2nd Revolution\nMuch like the first revolution, the nationalists take up arms against the tyrannical globalist government in hopes to secure not only their way of life but also the bring back the american dream that has been strangled by the elites of the social order.\n","x":-360,"y":28189,"width":349,"height":189},
		{"id":"e8dfff2ed112fdfc","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2030) City Riots.md","x":109,"y":28683,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ba76fd90f7f7c616","type":"text","text":"Targeted Infrastructure\nMany of the nationalists cells flee the inner cities and start a guerrilla war. The nationalists first goal is to begin a choke hold on the cities by destroying vital infrastructure such as bridges, train stations and the power grid substations.\n","x":-351,"y":28445,"width":331,"height":238},
		{"id":"1012a9e195b74389","type":"text","text":"Border Shutdown\nA boarder shutdown can be a particularly significant aspect of an artificial economic collapse caused by sudo national quarantines. If a government decides to shut down its borders as a way to contain the spread of disease, it can have far-reaching consequences for the economy and international relations. In practice, a boarder shutdown can involve restrictions on travel between countries, including bans on flights, train and bus services, and land border crossings. These restrictions can have a severe impact on trade, tourism, and other sectors of the economy that rely on international mobility. For example, a country may be highly dependent on exports of goods or services to other countries, and a boarder shutdown could disrupt these trade flows and create significant economic disruption. Similarly, international travelers may be an important source of revenue for the tourism industry, and a boarder shutdown could significantly reduce this revenue stream. A boarder shutdown can also have significant political implications, particularly if it is seen as a form of economic protectionism or xenophobia. Other countries may respond by imposing similar restrictions on their own borders, leading to further economic and diplomatic disruption. In addition, a boarder shutdown can have humanitarian consequences, particularly for individuals who are stranded abroad or unable to return home. This can create stress and anxiety for families and loved ones who are separated by the quarantine, as well as increased strain on social services and other support systems. Overall, a boarder shutdown is a potentially catastrophic response to a sudo national quarantine. Governments must carefully weigh the economic and diplomatic consequences of such a measure before taking action, and consider alternative approaches to addressing the spread of disease that do not involve disrupting international trade and travel.\n","x":1040,"y":28262,"width":428,"height":442},
		{"id":"956ecdd5733e8059","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2030) Psychic surgery.md","x":509,"y":28683,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"139dcf263bd15e7d","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2032) Duel maternity.md","x":509,"y":29083,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c29039617690a840","type":"text","text":"Fires of Liberty\nWith Globalist cities set ablaze the nationalists army moved in and began to capture cities moving ever closer to the capital.\n","x":-333,"y":28760,"width":295,"height":186},
		{"id":"4ebfebb2a6bdf18d","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2032) Operation Home Run.md","x":109,"y":29083,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ec2bdc44534c1555","type":"text","text":"Political Executions\nThe end of an American civil war, which was marked by political upheaval and economic collapse, may lead to the implementation of political executions. In such a scenario, the victorious side of the war would seek to establish a new political order and eliminate any opposition that might challenge their rule. Political executions could take place in various forms, including summary trials, public hangings or beheadings, or targeted assassinations. These executions could target not only political leaders or military commanders who were on the losing side of the war, but also anyone who was perceived as a threat to the new government. For example, the political establishment could use the pretext of national security to eliminate potential dissidents or activists who posed a threat to their power. This could involve targeting individuals who were associated with social movements or protest groups that challenged the new regime's authority. The executions could be carried out in a highly public manner, as a way of sending a message to the population that dissent would not be tolerated. This could involve staging elaborate spectacles, with large crowds gathered to witness the punishment of those who were deemed to have committed crimes against the state. In addition to executions, the new government may also engage in other forms of coercion and intimidation to consolidate its power. This could include repressive policies that limit free speech and expression, suppress dissenting media outlets, and control public discourse. Overall, the end of an American civil war could be a time of great instability and upheaval, during which political executions could play a significant role in establishing a new political order. Such executions could have far-reaching consequences for the legacy of the conflict and for the future of American democracy.\n","x":-333,"y":29083,"width":330,"height":310},
		{"id":"3e245a17bd3ba686","type":"text","text":"End of the Revolution\nWith the fall of D.C the remaining globalist forces accepted unconditional surrender and were taken to various prisons to await military tribunal. With the Nationalists not in control of the country they soon put plans in motion to rebuild the war torn nation.\n","x":-720,"y":29120,"width":305,"height":237},
		{"id":"487298398e246cd7","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2034) Rebearth of a Nation.md","x":109,"y":29483,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"dd57b0388bce7f52","type":"text","text":"We The People\nThe constitution now revitalized holds new amendments which will prevent the federal government from becoming what it had prior to the revolution.\n","x":-326,"y":29483,"width":323,"height":161},
		{"id":"8a8e4f7dbecb7a68","type":"text","text":"Censorship\nModern-day censorship refers to the act of controlling or suppressing the flow of information and ideas in a particular society or government. This can include monitoring and controlling media content, restricting access to information, and punishing individuals who speak out against the government or its policies. Censorship can be enforced by various means, including laws and regulations, surveillance, and intimidation tactics. It can also take place through self-censorship, where individuals and organizations avoid speaking out or publishing information that could be considered controversial or offensive. The impact of censorship can be severe, with individuals and communities being restricted in their ability to express themselves, learn new ideas, and engage in free speech. This can have negative consequences for the democratic process, freedom of expression, and the ability of individuals to participate fully in society. Censorship is often justified by governments on the grounds of national security, public order, or cultural sensitivity. However, many argue that censorship undermines democratic values and promotes authoritarianism and control. There are several efforts to combat censorship, including advocacy groups that work to promote free speech and the protection of human rights. Some governments have also taken steps to ease restrictions on information and communication, although these measures can be limited and reversed by political pressure or economic factors. Overall, censorship remains a significant issue in many parts of the world, and efforts are ongoing to promote freedom of expression, transparency, and accountability in government.\n","x":640,"y":25600,"width":421,"height":390},
		{"id":"606274557a35eb46","type":"text","text":"Suppression\nBefore crucial elections the globalists made preparations to ensure that they maintain control. Such methods include bypassing the electoral college and changing state demographics. \n","x":-240,"y":26342,"width":243,"height":276},
		{"id":"688d621a1f6ed1e9","type":"text","text":"Bioregionalism\nBioregionalism is a political, cultural, and ecological philosophy that emphasizes living in harmony with the natural characteristics of a specific geographic area—called a bioregion—rather than artificial boundaries like national or state borders.\n\nCore Principles of Bioregionalism:\nNatural Boundaries over Political Ones\nBioregions are defined by watersheds, landforms, soil types, climate zones, and native species, not by human-imposed lines on a map.\n\nLocal Self-Sufficiency\nEmphasizes locally based economies, agriculture, and energy systems tailored to the ecological capacities of the region.\n\nCultural Reconnection\nAdvocates for resurrecting or preserving place-based languages, traditions, and knowledge systems, recognizing that culture and ecology are intertwined.\n\nDecentralized Governance\nSupports community autonomy and grassroots decision-making, often in opposition to globalization or federal centralization.\n\nEcological Stewardship\nEncourages sustainable interaction with the environment, treating humans as participants in rather than masters of their ecosystems.\n\nIn Practice:\nIt may manifest as regional food sovereignty, watershed-based policy, eco-village design, or resistance to transnational development projects.\n\nOften aligns with movements like permaculture, degrowth, eco-anarchism, or post-globalist democracy.\n","x":-739,"y":25964,"width":419,"height":516},
		{"id":"eeb6a6eabfd81c23","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Pre-WW3/Faction Profile/UAR/UAR.md","x":109,"y":29883,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e1b0cd77e5258d23","type":"text","text":"Seal of the UAR\n![[C543A705-FCE2-4896-8F1B-B9A102E85076.png]]\nA bald eagle in the form of a phoenix replaces the old seal.\n1. The Eagle Was a Symbol of Stability\n\nThe eagle on the U.S. Seal stood for:\n\t•\tcontinuity\n\t•\tthe same republic from 1776 to now\n\t•\tEnlightenment values\n\t•\tfederal power restrained by law\n\t•\tterritorial guardianship\n\t•\tsovereignty instead of conquest\n\nThe eagle is old-world.\nIt implies the country is still the same nation it was founded to be.\n\nAfter a civil war that dismantles the federal bureaucracy, destroys cities, and rewrites the Constitution, the eagle no longer fits reality.\n\nThe nation that comes afterward cannot pretend it is the same.\n\n⸻\n\n2. The Phoenix Represents a Complete Break With the Old Republic\n\nThe phoenix implies:\n\t•\tdeath → resurrection → transformation\n\t•\tidentity rebirth\n\t•\tthe fire that purifies\n\t•\ta new cycle, not a continuation\n\t•\tsurvival through destruction\n\nThe Nationalist victory isn’t reform.\nIt’s rebirth through fire.\n\nThe phoenix is the only symbol that doesn’t lie.\n\nIt tells the world:\n\n“The United States died.\nWhat stands before you is new.”\n\nThis parallels the broader theme in your alt-history:\ninstitutions don’t reform — they collapse, and then something else stands up from the ashes.\n\n⸻\n\n3. A Phoenix Fits a Hemisphere-Wide Republic Better Than an Eagle\n\nThe eagle is tied to nation-state America.\n\nThe UAR is:\n\t•\tcontinental\n\t•\tpost-national\n\t•\tpost-democratic (in the old sense)\n\t•\tmilitarized\n\t•\tculturally composite\n\t•\tforged in collapse\n\t•\tideologically hardened\n\nIt needs a symbol that:\n\t•\ttranscends regional identity\n\t•\tcommands loyalty across the hemisphere\n\t•\tjustifies the absorption of Canada, Mexico, and South America\n\t•\timplies unity through shared trauma\n\t•\tframes the UAR as the rebuilder of civilization\n\nA phoenix is universal.\nEvery culture can read themselves into it.\n\nThat makes it ideal for a mega-state.\n\n⸻\n\n4. The Phoenix Also Has a Psychological Function for a Traumatized Population\n\nAfter the Second Civil War, Americans experience:\n\t•\tnational shame\n\t•\texhaustion\n\t•\tgrief\n\t•\tshattered civic identity\n\t•\tideological disorientation\n\t•\tdistrust of institutions\n\nA new symbol acts like a psychological reset:\n\t•\tfresh start\n\t•\tnew mission\n\t•\tcollective identity that isn’t tied to the failures of the old republic\n\t•\tpermission to move forward without looking back\n\t•\tjustification for harsh reconstruction policies\n\nThe phoenix gives emotional coherence to a broken nation.\n\n⸻\n\n5. The Phoenix Signals a Return to Hard Power\n\nThe eagle carries Enlightenment restraint.\n\nThe phoenix carries mythic inevitability.\n\nA phoenix doesn’t negotiate.\nA phoenix endures.\n\nThis fits the Nationalist-controlled UAR that:\n\t•\tremoves foreign influence\n\t•\tcloses borders\n\t•\tmilitarizes continental defense\n\t•\teliminates PMCs\n\t•\tpurges captured information systems\n\t•\tenforces civil reconstruction\n\t•\texpands into the entire hemisphere without apology\n\nIt also marks a shift from:\n\nsoft, moralizing Western liberalism → hard, survivalist continental realism\n\nThat shift is core to the UAR’s identity.\n\n⸻\n\n6. The Phoenix Makes the UAR a “Post-Collapse Civilization”\n\nThis is important for the wider Dominion/Severance meta-lore.\n\nA post-collapse civilization:\n\t•\tdoesn’t pretend continuity\n\t•\tknows collapse was unavoidable\n\t•\tviews itself as chosen by survival\n\t•\tbuilds its identity around endurance\n\t•\tsees borders as existential\n\t•\tsees unity as life-or-death\n\t•\tsees dissent as entropy\n\t•\tsees history as a cycle, not a straight line\n\nA phoenix civilization is built for the Severance era.\n\nIt’s harder.\nColder.\nMore cohesive.\nLess sentimental.\n\nMore prepared for what’s coming.\n\n⸻\n\n7. The Phoenix Is Also a Warning\n\nA phoenix is not a dove.\n\nIt tells rival blocs:\n\n“We have died once.\nWe will not die again.”\n\nCRINK reads this as a declaration of militarized revival.\nEuropolis sees it as “the rise of authoritarian Americana.”\nLatin states (absorbed or stabilized) see it as a promise:\n“Your collapses will not kill you — we will rebuild you, for better or worse.”\n\nIt strikes fear.\nWhich is the point\n","x":669,"y":29825,"width":480,"height":516},
		{"id":"cac42bc21d3d8e27","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Historical Eras/I - Lithic Era. (Origins)/(2035) Corruption of the European Union.md","x":109,"y":30283,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a19e250ba3465a51","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Pre-WW3/Faction Profile/Yamama Caliphate/Yamama Caliphate.md","x":109,"y":30683,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cec37a82891e3c49","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Pre-WW3/Faction Profile/Yamama Caliphate/Abdulrahman bin Ali Al-Saud.md","x":669,"y":30683,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"3c9a00ad26b035d8","type":"text","text":"Land of the Caliphate\nIf the Middle East were under the control of a Caliphate, it would have access to a range of resources within the region, including: 1. Oil and natural gas: The Middle East is home to some of the world's largest oil and natural gas reserves, which would be a valuable asset for the Caliphate. 2. Agricultural resources: The Middle East has a diverse range of agricultural resources, including wheat, rice, fruits, and vegetables, which could be used to feed the population and exported to other countries. 3. Minerals: The Middle East is also home to significant mineral resources, such as iron ore, copper, and gold, which could be used for industrial and commercial purposes. 4. Tourism: The Middle East is a popular tourist destination, with many historical and cultural sites of interest. This could provide an additional source of revenue for the Caliphate through tourism and travel industries. 5. Transportation: The Middle East has a well-developed transportation infrastructure, including airports, ports, and highways, which could be used to facilitate trade and commerce between countries. 6. Human resources: The Middle East has a large and skilled workforce, which could be used to support various economic activities within the region. Overall, a Caliphate in the Middle East would have access to a range of resources that could be used to promote economic growth and development, as well as enhance its military and political power in the region.\n","x":1149,"y":30707,"width":417,"height":353},
		{"id":"6bba6114d12914de","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Economy & Infrastructure/Locations/Countries/Iran.md","x":909,"y":31200,"width":400,"height":400},
